SUMMARY:Storytime with Sujji Ajji
DESCRIPTION:\nInspired by real conversations with her granddaughter\, and her debut picture book We Are Family\, Sujatha Balakrishnan creates a warm and welcoming space for children to celebrate different kinds of families. Through storytelling\, conversation and playful activities\, the session aims to normalise conversations around adoption with openness\, curiosity and empathy\, helping children discover that love is what truly makes a family. \nAround the World in 50 Sundays is a journey that begins\, not with a ticket\, but with opening a book. In a city like Bangalore where families are always in motion\, the BIC Library hopes to offer stillness and a quiet\, welcoming space for both parents and children where reading becomes a shared experience. Every Sunday\, we open our doors to invite you into a library that listens; building a rhythm of return\, a habit of joy and a new community bound not just by books\, but by the weekly ritual of reading together.  \nWe welcome your ideas and input. If you have suggestions for children’s events or activities that align with this vision\, we’d love to hear from you. Please reach out to us at library@bangaloreinternationalcentre.org \nSupported by:\n \n\n\n\nStories\, Belonging and Hearts That Grow\nFor Ages 5-10 (Accompanied by Parent/Caregiver)\nRSVPs closed. Thank you for your interest.\n*Facilitator*: Sujatha Balakrishnan\n*Event Categories*: Around the World in 50 Sundays\, Children's Books
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/storytime-with-sujji-ajji/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Around the World in 50 Sundays,Children's Books
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Thumbnail_SWSA.png
END:VEVENT
