SUMMARY:Crystal & Ash
DESCRIPTION:Are relics more than static remnants of the past? \nThis lecture on the relics of the Buddha excavated from the ancient stupa at Piprahwa\, traces their long\, contested journey to reveal the deep entanglement of material culture\, belief\, and power across history and into the present. \nExcavated in 1898 and removed from India for over a century\, the Piprahwa relics have been shrouded in controversy\, from disputes over authenticity to competing claims of ownership and attempted auctions. Their recent return brings new urgency to old questions. Naman P. Ahuja will explain how relics are defined in Buddhist tradition\, their role in geopolitics through what scholars call “relic diplomacy\,” the legal shifts shaping their custody\, and what all this means for museums today. \nImage Credit: Jewel relics of the Buddha on view at the exhibition Lotus & the Light\, New Delhi 2026. \nVenue: Auditorium\n\n\nThe Buddha at Piprahwa\nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScX1wUXzu_Y5_394Ggloe4BUNNYyBNSqUhk8L-SOU1FMXcYzg/viewform?usp=pp_url)\n*Speaker*: Naman P Ahuja\n*Event Categories*: Books\, Faith\, Heritage\, Nonfiction\, Visual Arts
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/crystal-ash/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Books,Faith,Heritage,Nonfiction,Visual Arts
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Thumbnail_CA.jpg
